{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_core_metrics", "label": "Core metrics", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsextension", "label": "MetricsExtension", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exposes the three primitives and holds the registry. Until enable is called the registry is a noop, and DevTools is the one thing that switches it on for you while attached."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_counter", "label": "Counter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monotonic - negative increments throw, and it resets on process restart. For things that go down, use a gauge."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_gauge", "label": "Gauge", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Settable and bidirectional; represents a point-in-time value such as active sessions, mailbox depth or queue size."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_histogram", "label": "Histogram", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Counts how many observations fell into each bucket, from which Prometheus computes percentiles at query time. There is no dedicated timer primitive - observe an elapsed duration instead."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_histogram_buckets", "label": "Histogram bucket choice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pick buckets that capture your SLO, bias toward fewer in the noise floor and more around the target; the defaults are seconds-scale and need overriding for millisecond-scale observations."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_labels", "label": "Metric labels", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Turn one metric into many time-series - each unique label combination is a separate series, read in Prometheus or Grafana as filters or group-by axes."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_cardinality_discipline", "label": "Cardinality discipline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unbounded labels such as a request id, a user id or a timestamp produce unbounded series and your monitoring system runs out of memory. Bounded labels only - route names, environment, status kinds, pod names where the pod count is bounded - and aim for under 100 series per metric."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_bucketize", "label": "bucketize", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Maps a value that comes from outside onto a fixed allow-list before it reaches the registry, returning the value when it is allowed and other otherwise - so the family can never hold more series than the allow-list length plus one, no matter what an attacker sends."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_cardinality_cap", "label": "Per-family cardinality cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "bucketize is the fix; the cap is the backstop for the labels nobody bounded. A family stops minting series at maxSeriesPerFamily and folds the rest into one overflow series, warning once per family rather than per call. The marker lives in the label value, not a label name, because Prometheus reserves double-underscore label names and strips them at ingestion, which would silently merge the overflow into a real series. The default is 10 000 rather than the ~1 000 that would look sufficient, because an incident is exactly when the widest families are at their widest and exactly when you need to read them."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsregistryoptions", "label": "MetricsRegistryOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Raises or disables the cap when the registry is installed; 0 disables it - 0 rather than Infinity, because the cap is an integer count."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_noop_registry", "label": "Noop metrics registry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The default until enable is called: the framework own instrumentation resolves against it and records nothing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_reading_values_in_process", "label": "Reading metric values in-process", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "value is a readonly property rather than a method; histograms expose count, sum, buckets and counts directly - useful for tests and custom exporters."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_core_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_metricsextension", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_core_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_counter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_core_metrics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_gauge", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/metrics/core-metrics.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_metrics_core_metrics_core_metrics", 